<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
<p class="meta">Tileshire &nbsp;·&nbsp; Effective date: June 10, 2026</p>

<p>
  This Privacy Policy describes how Tileshire (the "App") handles your information.
  The short version: <strong>Tileshire does not collect, transmit, or share any personal data.</strong>
</p>

<h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
<p>
  Tileshire does not collect any personal information. The App stores game progress
  (high scores, run state, and settings) locally on your device using standard device
  storage. This data never leaves your device and is not accessible to us.
</p>

<h2>2. Third-Party Services</h2>
<p>
  Tileshire does not use any third-party analytics, advertising, crash-reporting,
  or data-collection services.
</p>

<h2>3. Internet Permissions</h2>
<p>
  The App does not require an internet connection and does not transmit any data
  over the network.
</p>

<h2>4. Children's Privacy</h2>
<p>
  Tileshire does not knowingly collect any information from anyone, including children
  under the age of 13. Because no data is collected at all, the App is safe for
  players of all ages.
</p>

<h2>5. Data Deletion</h2>
<p>
  All locally stored data (saves, high scores, settings) can be deleted at any time
  by uninstalling the App or clearing the App's data in your device settings.
</p>

<h2>6. Changes to This Policy</h2>
<p>
  If this policy changes, the updated version will be posted at this URL with a new
  effective date. We encourage you to review it periodically.
</p>

<h2>7. Contact</h2>
<p>
  If you have any questions about this Privacy Policy, please contact:<br />
  <a href="mailto:antonbargman@gmail.com">antonbargman@gmail.com</a>
</p>

</body>
